00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.220
A tissue study of 28 women found ovaries still change after menopause. This is Longevity Weekly Episode 5. The science of aging, read carefully, never medical advice. After that finding, a tablet in development for older dogs, posts about an unapproved weight loss drug, a mouse study on bone, and a mechanism segment on how to read longevity evidence. The Buck Institute and Northwestern looked at ovarian tissue and found proteins, inflammation, and tissue structure still shifting.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:35.080
That work is a laboratory study of human tissue, not a randomized trial, and it tested neither

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.440
a drug nor a behavior.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.160
The report says those shifts raise new questions about women's health as they age.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.300
It does not describe a regulator approving any treatment from this work.

00:00:46.201 --> 00:00:50.741
Loyal, a San Francisco company, has cleared two of three major technical sections the

00:00:50.741 --> 00:00:54.941
Food and Drug Administration requires before it can conditionally approve a tablet called

00:00:55.961 --> 00:00:56.541
Loy002.

00:00:56.541 --> 00:01:02.781
Yahoo Creators describes that tablet as once daily for dogs aged 10 and older that way

00:01:02.781 --> 00:01:04.041
at least 14 pounds.

00:01:04.621 --> 00:01:09.761
The article says the pill could reach clinics as early as late 2026 or 2027.

00:01:10.561 --> 00:01:15.021
Veterinarian Rebecca Greenstein told that outlet the aim is better insulin sensitivity

00:01:15.021 --> 00:01:19.381
and lower insulin and a longer health span rather than frozen age.

00:01:19.841 --> 00:01:24.061
She cited a 14-year Purina feeding experiment published in 2002.

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:30.701
Labrador retrievers given 25% fewer calories than litter mates stayed leaner, got chronic disease

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:36.801
later, and lived a median of nearly two years longer. That calorie result is an animal experiment,

00:01:37.041 --> 00:01:43.081
not a human trial, and not a test of Loy 002, and the American Animal Hospital Association

00:01:43.081 --> 00:01:54.323
classes 44% of pets as seniors. Reddit Trutide, an unapproved weight loss drug, was the subject of a

00:01:54.323 --> 00:02:00.223
med page today reported. The words those users cited most often were appetite increases, fatigue,

00:02:00.823 --> 00:02:06.943
increased energy, insomnia, a faster heart rate, and muscle symptoms. Those are online self-reports,

00:02:07.243 --> 00:02:12.583
not a randomized trial, so they cannot say how often any of that happens or what was actually in

00:02:12.583 --> 00:02:18.683
hand. Nothing in that report says a regulator has approved retitrutide for any use, aging related

00:02:18.683 --> 00:02:19.503
or otherwise.

00:02:20.517 --> 00:02:25.337
Marrow fat cells in aging mice sent sting signals tied to inflammation and to falling

00:02:25.337 --> 00:02:27.677
NAD plus in the cells that build bone.

00:02:28.437 --> 00:02:32.877
Lifespan.io reports that interrupting that pathway helped keep aging bone.

00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:37.657
That is a mouse experiment, and the summary does not describe approval of any related

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:38.637
approach for people.

00:02:39.731 --> 00:02:43.251
How to read longevity evidence starts with a mismatch from 2014.

00:02:43.251 --> 00:02:48.391
Dealing in colleagues in human molecular genetics published a genome-wide

00:02:48.391 --> 00:02:54.231
association study of human longevity that a cell cycle commentary called the largest to that date.

00:02:54.711 --> 00:03:00.331
Gene's already known to stretch life a great deal in rodents were not consistently linked to human longevity

00:03:00.331 --> 00:03:03.931
in that scan or in association studies more generally.

00:03:04.471 --> 00:03:11.591
A rodent experiment can show that one genetic change in one strain changes lifespan or changes a pathway in tissue.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:17.351
A human genome-wide association study can show which variants travel statistically with

00:03:17.351 --> 00:03:19.691
a longevity phenotype in the people enrolled.

00:03:20.171 --> 00:03:25.351
A hit in one of those designs is not a cause proven in the other species, and neither design

00:03:25.351 --> 00:03:26.591
is a test of a treatment.

00:03:27.191 --> 00:03:30.951
The commentary lays out three explanations and does not crown one.

00:03:31.551 --> 00:03:36.871
Association studies have built-in limits, so even a large human scan can miss a real effect.

00:03:36.871 --> 00:03:42.871
human longevity may also be spread across many variants, so a gene with a big effect in a mouse

00:03:42.871 --> 00:03:48.831
need not show up as a clean hit in people. The author's own hypothesis puts part of the blame on the

00:03:48.831 --> 00:03:53.131
animal work. Most of those studies use strains with little genetic diversity,

00:03:53.491 --> 00:03:57.731
so a result in one narrow background may not apply to mixed human populations.

00:03:58.411 --> 00:04:02.151
The commentary also points to other results, not named in the abstract,

00:04:02.151 --> 00:04:06.771
where caloric restriction changed rodent lifespan in a strain-specific way.

00:04:07.331 --> 00:04:12.051
The translation question follows from that, genetics of aging findings may not move

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:16.971
cleanly into human therapies, and the commentary does not claim that move is impossible.

00:04:17.651 --> 00:04:22.911
The snail dwarf mouse carries a pit-1 mutation, and its long life has been tied to reduced

00:04:22.911 --> 00:04:26.391
insulin, IGF-1, and growth hormone signaling.

00:04:26.391 --> 00:04:32.671
cooling. Those hormones, plus thyroid stimulating hormone, help set protein synthesis rates, which

00:04:32.671 --> 00:04:38.531
fall in old rodent tissues. Earlier work had found PI-3K activity sharply lower in

00:04:38.531 --> 00:04:45.291
snow dwarf liver, and PI-3K helps control translation. The 2004 study compared young and

00:04:45.291 --> 00:04:51.911
aged snow dwarf livers and found less phosphorylation and less kinase activity of act, also called

00:04:51.911 --> 00:04:58.891
PKB and of P38MAPK, plus less phosphorylation of the downstream regulators of translation.

00:04:59.471 --> 00:05:04.651
The authors propose that lower protein synthesis may be an important feature of the pit-1 mutation

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.831
and of this mouse's long life.

00:05:07.251 --> 00:05:12.551
That is biochemistry in one long-lived mutant strain, not a human genetic association

00:05:12.551 --> 00:05:14.071
and not a randomized trial.

00:05:14.671 --> 00:05:18.451
Those liver readings may be exactly the kind of result that does not travel.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:25.331
Lower activity at several nodes of insulin and IGF-1 signaling, and of P-38MAP signaling,

00:05:25.831 --> 00:05:28.151
and lower marks of translational initiation.

00:05:28.791 --> 00:05:33.431
A kinase reading is a molecular measurement, not evidence that blocking the same node

00:05:33.431 --> 00:05:34.691
would lengthen human life.

00:05:35.251 --> 00:05:40.231
A missing association does not prove the pathway is irrelevant in people, and it does not

00:05:40.231 --> 00:05:41.531
prove the pathway matters.

00:05:42.211 --> 00:05:47.171
Neither paper is a randomized human trial, and neither reports that a regulator has approved

00:05:47.171 --> 00:05:54.991
reduced insulin or IGF-1 signaling, P-38-MAPK modulation, or any related approach for an aging-related

00:05:54.991 --> 00:06:01.151
use. Neither reports human safety results. What they do support is a limit, a lifespan difference

00:06:01.151 --> 00:06:07.331
in a low-diversity mouse strain, or a drop in liver kinase activity, is not evidence that a therapy

00:06:07.331 --> 00:06:13.091
will work in humans. The strongest human side-finding is a negative one, and the commentary states

00:06:13.091 --> 00:06:18.691
its own limit. Rodent lifespan genes were not consistently associated with human longevity in

00:06:18.691 --> 00:06:23.651
the largest genome-wide study than available, or in association studies more generally.

00:06:24.231 --> 00:06:29.111
And that gap does not say whether the biology fails in people, or whether the studies could not

00:06:29.111 --> 00:06:35.087
have shown the link. One thing worth knowing is that a lab study of ovarian tissue can show menopause

00:06:35.087 --> 00:06:40.747
is not a full biological stop in that organ, and still cannot show that any product changes those

00:06:40.747 --> 00:06:46.007
features. Another is that symptom words posted after an unapproved drug mark use outside

00:06:46.007 --> 00:06:52.387
a trial, not account of how often harm occurs. That's longevity weekly. This show is education,

